  "caption": "A low-speed nudge at the lights, everyone okay, but the next day Quinn's neck was stiff and sore. Quinn's plan: hold perfectly still.\n\nMost whiplash is a soft-tissue strain that tends to recover well. Gentle early movement often helps more than resting in a collar, and worry about moving can slow things down.\n\nWhat can help: move your neck within comfort several times a day, keep up short walks and normal activity, build range and then deep neck and shoulder-blade strength step by step, and return to work as you're able.\n\nGet checked promptly for arm numbness or weakness, trouble walking or with coordination, a severe unusual headache, dizziness with double vision, or if you lost consciousness.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
